/* Cross-ISO mechanism matrix — SOCO shard (rule 28 [R-MECH-MATRIX]).
 *
 * This file is SOCO's COLUMN of the matrix: one line per mechanism id
 * (the row set lives in ../mechanism-matrix.js, which carries the
 * mechanism-level id/cat/name/def/mode/note). A session that tests a
 * mechanism in SOCO updates ONLY this file — the cell verdict, the
 * forecast-lane posture (fc), the evidence citation (ev) and any
 * SOCO-specific note — plus the keeper/gates stamps on promotion.
 * Never edit another ISO's shard (rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE]): a verdict
 * transfers to no other ISO; candidates enter the target shard as U.
 *
 * SOCO is a BALANCING AUTHORITY, not an ISO — the Southern Company
 * footprint (Alabama Power / Georgia Power / Mississippi Power), keyed
 * `SOCO` after the EIA-930/EIA-860 BA code (owner card S1, ruled
 * 2026-09-13). It is vertically integrated and cost-based: no LMP, no
 * capacity auction, no ancillary-service market, no offer cap. That is
 * why this column carries more `.` than any RTO's, and every one of them
 * names the ruling or gate it rests on.
 *
 * Cell codes (same vocabulary as the base header): K keeper, R rejected,
 * I inert, G governance-refused/closed, O open, U untested, . n/a.
 * `fc` is the forecast-lane posture where it DIFFERS from the backcast
 * cell (omitted = same as cell). `ev` is this ISO's evidence citation.
 *
 * SEEDED AT SOCO-21 (2026-09-13), the eighth shard — mechanical emission,
 * NO VERDICT MINTED. SOCO has no keeper, no registered run and no solve of
 * any kind at HEAD, so `keeper` and `gates` are deliberately EMPTY and every
 * cell is `U` (untested, plausibly applicable) or `.` (structurally n/a).
 * An 8-ISO matrix over a 7-ISO registry is a supported intermediate state:
 * SOCO-20 registers the ISO, and neither scripts/lib/mech_matrix.py nor
 * scripts/check_mechanism_matrix.py reads SUPPORTED_ISOS or _ISO_BUILDERS —
 * the same order SPP ran in (column seeded SPP-21 2026-09-06, first keeper
 * SPP-40). Charter: docs/multi-iso/soco-addition-plan-2026-09.md §5 row
 * SOCO-21 (the W5 lever queue it seeds is §4 there and
 * docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.8); record
 * docs/handoffs/FINDING-soco-21-2026-09-13.md.
 *
 * THE CLASSIFICATION RULE, applied in order (so a later lane can audit any
 * cell without re-deriving the whole column):
 *   (a) ISO-EXCLUSIVE ELSEWHERE -> `.` — the row names another ISO's own
 *       market object (a foreign ScenarioConfig field stem, or a foreign
 *       region/programme name: wtx_ path15_ wecc_ tsa_ rdt_tcdc) AND no
 *       non-owner ISO has entered the cell at HEAD. A foreign-stemmed row
 *       that some OTHER ISO HAS entered is a live cross-ISO question, so
 *       SOCO reads `U` there, not `.` (e.g. ercot_wind_zone_shape,
 *       miso_intermediate_gas_offer_margin, pjm_midcurve_belt). `spp_*` is
 *       foreign here too — SPP is the seventh column, not this one.
 *   (b) NO CENTRALIZED CAPACITY MARKET -> `.` — the object is a cleared
 *       capacity price, its VRR/FCA/RBDC or locality demand curve, its
 *       sell-offer-stack clearing, its published default-ACR offer-cap
 *       convention, or its net-CONE vintages. Card S6 (ruled 2026-09-13)
 *       registers SOCO ABSENT from MARKET_DESIGN / _CURVE_ISOS /
 *       _CAPACITY_ISOS. SIX rows: capacity_market_clearing,
 *       capacity_market_supply_clearing, capacity_going_forward_bar_published,
 *       capacity_no_default_cap_convention, net_cone_forward_vintages,
 *       locality_capacity_curves.
 *   (c) NO CLEARED ANCILLARY-SERVICE MARKET -> `.` — the object is an in-LP
 *       reserve row, its published requirement/demand curve, or the dual that
 *       prices it. SOCO clears no AS market and takes no offers (card S5), and
 *       the registration carries co_opt=False. FOUR rows:
 *       energy_reserve_coopt, reserve_pergen, dynamic_reserve_requirements,
 *       reserve_deliverability_scoping. The two reserve SIDECAR rows stay `U`:
 *       they are CROSS-ISO INSTRUMENT rows (write-only bundle artifacts every
 *       run emits), so the object exists for SOCO even when it is empty, and
 *       what it holds is SOCO-40's to measure.
 *   (d) NO SCARCITY PRICING / NO OFFER CAP -> `.` — card S5, ruled: "No ORDC,
 *       no scarcity seed"; there is no market to cap. ONE row:
 *       ordc_scarcity_overlay.
 *   (e) NO CARBON PROGRAMME -> `.` — the object is a state/regional carbon
 *       programme (RGGI / CA cap-and-trade); no state in SOCO's footprint
 *       (AL / GA / MS) carries one and the registration is carbon-`None`
 *       (gate G7). ONE row: state_carbon_pricing.
 *   otherwise -> `U`.
 * `.` is the STRONGER claim (it forecloses a lever), so every row this
 * session could not place with a stated structural reason falls through to
 * `U`, the weaker one — including rows whose applicability is genuinely open
 * (capacity_deliverability, reserve_margin_backstop,
 * adequacy_internal_supply_accounting, lcr_tsl_published, legacy_p2,
 * mass_cap_lp_row, m2m_seam_entitlement_cap, online_capacity_envelope,
 * measured_ramp_capability). A later SOCO lane closes those on SOCO's own
 * data (rule 25), never by reading another column.
 *
 * TWO OF THE CHARTER'S FOUR `.` REASONS DELIBERATELY PRODUCE NO `.` CELL,
 * because the test the charter states is "structurally n/a for SOCO" and
 * neither of them meets it. Both are recorded on the affected rows' `ev`
 * instead, at full strength:
 *   - NO IMPORT NODE (gate G7 — neither IMPORT_TRANCHES["SOCO"] nor
 *     IMPORT_ZONE["SOCO"], so build_import_generators('SOCO') == []) is a
 *     REGISTRATION fact for the first keeper, whose seams are served measured
 *     EIA-930 interchange (card S4). The SAME ruling registers priced
 *     NeighborInterfaces default-off as lever SOCO-56, so `.` would foreclose
 *     a chartered lever. SIX rows read `U` carrying that fact:
 *     priced_interchange, reference_price_interface, import_hub_pricing,
 *     import_shape_lever, seam_neighbour_anchored_ladder,
 *     seam_neighbour_hourly_ladder.
 *   - NO OFFER-CURVE TUNING CHANNEL (gate G5 — the rule 1 [R-STRUCT]
 *     carve-out authorizes tuning MARKET OFFERS and SOCO takes none, so the
 *     bands stay 1.0 unless the owner rules otherwise) closes the AUTHORIZED
 *     PRICE-TUNING CHANNEL, not the row's object: SOCO's first keeper will
 *     carry per-class band curves at neutral 1.0, and the duty-role cohort
 *     splits registered on that row are live SOCO questions. ONE row reads
 *     `U` carrying that fact: offer_curve_by_group.
 *
 * Forecast-only rows (base `mode: "F"`) carry `cell: "."` — a forecast
 * mechanism has no backcast posture — plus `fc: "U"`. SOCO has NO
 * forecast-lane entry at HEAD: that is W6, routed to the capx director
 * (plan §3 card S10), and this shard is not the forecast board.
 *
 * Owner rulings already reflected in this seed: S1 (key `SOCO`, ev key "O"),
 * S4 (served measured EIA-930 interchange; priced seams = lever SOCO-56),
 * S5 (no ORDC, no scarcity seed; ICE-calculator VOLL), S6 (no capacity
 * market), all r#2/r#3 2026-09-13.
 *
 * Append SOCO column re-stamp history as block comments at the END of this
 * file.
 */
window.MECH_MATRIX_SHARDS = window.MECH_MATRIX_SHARDS || {};
